# Build context exclusions.
#
# Both images are built from the repo root, so this one file governs both the
# Python build (Dockerfile) and the dashboard build (apps/web/Dockerfile) --
# apps/web/.dockerignore is inert, because it only applies when the context is
# apps/web itself.
#
# Patterns are matched against the whole path from the context root, so a bare
# `node_modules/` would match only a top-level one and miss apps/web's. Every
# nested pattern needs the `**/` prefix.

# --- Secrets. Never in an image: a layer keeps them even if a later ---------
# --- layer deletes the file. -----------------------------------------------
.env
.env.local
**/.env
**/.env.local
**/*.local

# --- Host-built artefacts ---------------------------------------------------
# These are Windows binaries (sharp, the Next SWC toolchain) that break inside
# the Linux container. Excluding them also stops `COPY apps/web/ ./` from
# clobbering the Linux node_modules that the web image installs itself.
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/out
**/dist
**/.turbo
.venv/
venv/

# --- Caches -----------------------------------------------------------------
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
.coverage
htmlcov/

# --- Not needed at runtime --------------------------------------------------
.git/
.github/
docs/
.vscode/
.idea/
ForMe.txt

# --- OS ---------------------------------------------------------------------
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
**/desktop.ini
